Patch 0013: fix(#151) combining mark after wide char misplaced in both renderers

Root cause: in the glyph-position loop, each glyph's column was computed as
startColumn + (i * columnWidth). For a wide-char EGC with a combining mark,
Core Text produces 2+ glyphs (base + mark). The combining mark has zero advance
(ctPosition.x ≈ prev glyph position), so its true column is the same as the
base glyph. The i * columnWidth formula placed it at startColumn + columnWidth
instead — one full wide-cell offset, i.e. drawn over the next narrow cell (F10).
Fix: for wide-char segments (columnWidth >= 2), detect zero-advance glyphs by
comparing adjacent CT positions. When advance < 0.5 * cellWidth, pin the glyph
to the previous column. Regular CJK chars have advance ≈ 2 * cellWidth, unaffected.
Applied to both the Core Text path (AppleTerminalView.swift) and the Metal path
(MetalTerminalRenderer.swift) since both shared the same formula.

--- a/Sources/SwiftTerm/Apple/AppleTerminalView.swift
+++ b/Sources/SwiftTerm/Apple/AppleTerminalView.swift
@@ -1527,9 +1527,31 @@
                     CTRunGetPositions(run, CFRange(), &coreTextPositions)
 
                     var positions = [CGPoint](repeating: .zero, count: runGlyphsCount)
+                    // For wide-char segments (columnWidth >= 2), a combining mark after a
+                    // wide CJK glyph has zero CT advance and is drawn by CT at the SAME x
+                    // as its base glyph. Without a correction the column is computed as
+                    // startColumn + (i * columnWidth), placing the mark one full wide slot
+                    // past the base — drawn over the next narrow cell instead of the CJK
+                    // glyph (F10, #151). Patch 0013 detects combining glyphs by their
+                    // near-zero advance (< 0.5 × cellWidth) and pins them to the previous
+                    // glyph's column. Regular wide chars are unaffected: their CT advance
+                    // is ≈ columnWidth × cellWidth, well above the 0.5 threshold.
+                    var prevGlyphColumn = startColumn
                     for i in 0..<runGlyphsCount {
                         let ctPosition = coreTextPositions[i]
-                        let glyphColumn = startColumn + (i * prepared.segment.columnWidth)
+                        let glyphColumn: Int
+                        if prepared.segment.columnWidth >= 2 && i > 0 {
+                            let advance = ctPosition.x - coreTextPositions[i - 1].x
+                            if advance < 0.5 * cellDimension.width {
+                                // Zero-advance glyph (combining mark): draw over the base.
+                                glyphColumn = prevGlyphColumn
+                            } else {
+                                glyphColumn = startColumn + (i * prepared.segment.columnWidth)
+                            }
+                        } else {
+                            glyphColumn = startColumn + (i * prepared.segment.columnWidth)
+                        }
+                        prevGlyphColumn = glyphColumn
                         positions[i] = CGPoint(
                             x: lineOrigin.x + CGFloat(glyphColumn) * cellDimension.width,
                             y: lineOrigin.y + yOffset + ctPosition.y)
